,'The plan to reduce 12% GST on housing to a 5% without extending the benefit of input tax credit to developers will increase price of apartments (by The Times of India)...','','ਜਨਤਕ ਨੋਟਿਸ','Why reduced GST will prove costly for budget homebuyers (by The Times of India)','The plan to reduce 12% GST on housing to a 5% without extending the benefit of input tax credit to developers will increase price of apartments (by The Times of India)...','',1,'','https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/business/india-business/why-reduced-gst-will-prove-costly-for-budget-home-buyers/articleshow/67428239.cms','','','',2,1,'mngradminrera','2019-02-07 13:22:00.000','mngradminrera','2019-02-07 13:22:00.000'),(149,1014,'PB',0,'2019-02-14 00:00:00.000','News','Circular Notice','Builder fine Rs 1.5 lakh for failing to register sale agreement','MahaRERA fined a developer for not registering the sale agreement with a buyer. During a hearing when it was found that over ten years and the developer hadn\'t registered the agreement in spite of accepting over 10 per cent of the total consideration. It decided to penalize the developer and asked him to pay Rs 1.5 lakh to MahaRERA for the violation of section 13 which makes it mandatory to register the agreement once the buyer has paid 10 per cent of the total consideration to the developer.','','ਸਰਕੂਲਰ ਨੋਟਿਸ','Builder fine Rs 1.5 lakh for failing to register sale agreement','Builder fine Rs 1.5 lakh for failing to register sale agreement','',1,'','https://www.dnaindia.com/mumbai/report-mumbai-builder-fine-rs-15-lakh-for-failing-to-register-sale-agreement-2716643','https://www.dnaindia.com/mumbai/report-mumbai-builder-fine-rs-15-lakh-for-failing-to-register-sale-agreement-2716643','','',2,1,'admprogrammer.rera','2019-02-15 09:16:43.000','admprogrammer.rera','2019-02-15 09:16:43.000'),(150,1011,'PB',0,'2019-01-09 00:00:00.000','NA','Public Notice','Why reduced GST will prove costly for budget homebuyers (by The Times of India)','The plan to reduce 12%